        "text": "File Sharing Protocols\nThe Server Message Block (SMB) and NetBIOS protocols are the heart of file\nsharing in Microsoft Windows operating systems. The Samba protocol derives\nfrom SMB, and you will hear about those two terminologies interchangeably.\nNot only is Samba used in Windows OS, but it\u2019s widely used in Linux operating\nsystems to share files and for printing services.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 SMB (Port 445)\n\u2022 SNMP (Port UDP 161)\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
